description:
Three pre-existing v1-fallback divergences found by the s282b guard-edge battery (all byte-identical at pre-E1.1 HEAD, so not E1.1 regressions). All print the WRONG VALUE silently — no die, no gate:

1. Two blocks each declaring `my @dup` captured by a named sub → both subs see an empty array:
   { my @dup = ("a"); package E2A; sub g2a { $dup[0] } }
   { my @dup = ("b"); package E2B; sub g2b { $dup[0] } }
   print E2A::g2a(), E2B::g2b();   # perl: ab, PCL: (empty)

2. Block-scoped container capture returns the file-level global instead of the block lexical:
   our @blist = ("global");
   { my @blist = ("lex"); package E4; sub g4 { $blist[0] } }
   print E4::g4();   # perl: lex, PCL: global

3. Symbolic deref `@{$n}` sees the defvar'd file lexical (known v1 defvar artifact, may be a deliberate divergence — check docs before treating as a bug):
   my @dlist = (7); my $n = "dlist";
   { no strict "refs"; print scalar(@{$n}); }   # perl: 0, PCL: 1

Items 1–2 are the container siblings of the scalar block-static idiom that v2's extent-scoped _promote_captured already handles — the fix direction is to make v2 native-lower these (extent-scoped container promotion inside package-switching blocks) rather than patch v1. Part of the E1.2 capture-refusal burn-down (docs/v2-endgame-plan.md).
